  "agentSummary": "I inventoried 11 external APIs. I read the code directly instead of dispatching area readers, because the app's API usage sits in a handful of files. A few call sites are listed only by their first line, as noted below.\n\n- **Synth (`api.synthfinance.com`, raw HTTP via Faraday):** exchange rates, ticker search, ticker info and prices.\n  - Seven call sites are in `app/models/provider/synth.rb`: `/user`, `/rates/historical`, `/rates/historical-range`, `/tickers/search`, `/tickers/{symbol}` and `/tickers/{symbol}/open-close`.\n  - One more is in `lib/tasks/securities.rake`.\n  - The base URL can be overridden with `SYNTH_URL`. The API key comes from `SYNTH_API_KEY` or `Setting.synth_api_key`.\n- **Plaid (SDK, `plaid` 41.0.0):** bank linking and sync, through US and EU clients.\n  - `app/models/provider/plaid.rb` makes the production calls: link token, public token exchange, item, accounts, transactions sync, liabilities, institutions, investment holdings and investment transactions.\n  - `plaid_sandbox.rb` makes the sandbox calls.\n  - `lib/tasks/data_migration.rake` has a one-off `item_webhook_update`.\n- **Plaid webhooks:** `/webhooks/plaid` and `/webhooks/plaid_eu`, verified with the JWT `Plaid-Verification` header plus a body SHA256 check.\n- **Plaid Link JS:** the CDN script is loaded in `_head.html.erb` and used by `plaid_controller.js`. I recorded it under Plaid over HTTP.\n- **Stripe (SDK, `stripe` 15.3.0):** customers, checkout sessions, billing portal and events retrieve. It also uses `parse_thin_event` for signature checking and `subscriptions.list` in `lib/tasks/stripe.rake`. The webhook is `/webhooks/stripe`, handling `customer.subscription.*` events.\n- **OpenAI (SDK, `ruby-openai` 8.1.0):** `responses.create` for chat (`gpt-4.1`), auto-categorize and merchant detection (`gpt-4.1-mini`).\n- **GitHub (SDK, `octokit` 10.0.0):** latest release and markdown rendering, unauthenticated.\n- **Sentry (SDK, `sentry-ruby` 5.26.0):** error tracking, with `Sentry.capture_exception` used in about 25 places.\n  - I recorded the init, one webhook controller call, `sync.rb`, and `Sentry.set_user`.\n  - The remaining `capture_exception` calls are not recorded individually.\n- **Logtail (SDK, `logtail-rails`):** production log shipping when `LOGTAIL_API_KEY` is set.\n- **Intercom (SDK, `intercom-rails`):** the messenger widget, enabled when `INTERCOM_APP_ID` is set. It is recorded as config only.\n- **S3 and Cloudflare R2 (`aws-sdk-s3`):** ActiveStorage services in `config/storage.yml`, selected by `ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE`. These are config-only entries.\n- **`logo.synthfinance.com`:** the code only builds merchant logo URLs. The browser fetches them, so it is recorded as low-confidence.\n\nI did not record these:\n- Skylight is in the Gemfile, but I found no usage in code.\n- Doorkeeper makes the app an OAuth provider for other clients, not a consumer of an external API.\n- The app's own `/api/v1` endpoints are internal.\n- I found no arbitrary user-supplied URL fetching.\n- I did not read `lib/tasks/securities.rake` past line 45 or `lib/tasks/stripe.rake` past line 20, but a grep of `lib/**/*.rake` found no further provider calls.",
